WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.136 --> 00:00:13.796
do you mean?"

2
00:00:14.036 --> 00:00:15.077
Perda asked Maff.

3
00:00:15.697 --> 00:00:17.058
"How can it be your fault?"

4
00:00:17.078 --> 00:00:21.920
"Yeah, we're the ones who rescued Morb from that houseboat," Zann added.

5
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:26.522
"But I was the one who created the houseboat," Maff told them.

6
00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:29.263
"What?" Gliss exclaimed.

7
00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:32.124
"How?" Maff sighed.

8
00:00:32.704 --> 00:00:35.466
"I didn't want Wyssa to kill my brother," he said.

9
00:00:35.486 --> 00:00:37.668
"I know what Morb did.

10
00:00:38.368 --> 00:00:39.809
I know he deserved his fate.

11
00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:41.691
But he's my brother."

12
00:00:42.451 --> 00:00:44.032
His eyes had a faraway look.

13
00:00:44.052 --> 00:00:49.797
"Maybe if my brothers and sisters and I had been a little nicer to him, things would have

14
00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:50.417
been different.

15
00:00:51.438 --> 00:00:57.702
We should have included him more often, even though he was a Void Zann glanced at his friends.

16
00:00:57.723 --> 00:00:59.484
"Okay," he said.

17
00:01:00.204 --> 00:01:03.107
"But how did you stop Wyssa from doing what she planned to do?"

18
00:01:03.987 --> 00:01:04.808
Maff blinked.

19
00:01:04.828 --> 00:01:07.591
"Oh. That was easier than I expected.

20
00:01:08.311 --> 00:01:11.574
When she left Magica with Morb, I tracked her through the vortex."

21
00:01:11.594 --> 00:01:13.175
"You did?"

22
00:01:13.356 --> 00:01:13.876
Perda said.

23
00:01:13.896 --> 00:01:16.558
"How?" Maff shrugged.

24
00:01:16.578 --> 00:01:20.081
"I've made a lifelong study of off-world magic," he said.

25
00:01:20.101 --> 00:01:22.223
"I used a difficult spell."

26
00:01:23.564 --> 00:01:24.325
Zann nodded.

27
00:01:25.026 --> 00:01:27.408
He guessed that Maff was a very powerful Red.

28
00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:32.972
Otherwise he wouldn't be hanging around at the palace with Venna and the other important people in First

29
00:01:33.052 --> 00:01:38.056
City. "I expected the spell to lead me to Fardark," Maff went on.

30
00:01:38.677 --> 00:01:42.740
"That's a terrible world where—" "We know," Zann broke in.

31
00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:43.881
"We've been there."

32
00:01:44.822 --> 00:01:45.583
Perda shuddered.

33
00:01:45.603 --> 00:01:49.986
"Yes. Wyssa had threatened to feed Morb to a scatter beast."

34
00:01:50.987 --> 00:01:53.669
"I thought that was her plan too," Maff said.

35
00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:56.552
"But instead I ended up on Skellia."

36
00:01:57.552 --> 00:02:01.654
"So Ello—I mean Morb—was telling us the truth?"

37
00:02:01.974 --> 00:02:02.654
Gliss asked.

38
00:02:02.674 --> 00:02:06.556
"Wyssa brought Morb along when she rescued the Skellian people?"

39
00:02:06.576 --> 00:02:09.197
"Not exactly," Maff said.

40
00:02:09.217 --> 00:02:16.580
"Apparently she left him immobilized in an unpopulated world while she transported the Skellians to their new home.

41
00:02:17.481 --> 00:02:20.282
Then she retrieved Morb and brought him to Skellia."

42
00:02:21.302 --> 00:02:22.703
"Why?" Zann asked.

43
00:02:22.723 --> 00:02:24.944
"Did she want to feed him to a gulper?"

44
00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.413
Maff smiled faintly.

45
00:02:27.433 --> 00:02:29.855
"I doubt a gulper would be interested.

46
00:02:30.496 --> 00:02:31.837
Morb had no magic left."

47
00:02:31.857 --> 00:02:34.099
"Right," Darb said.

48
00:02:34.119 --> 00:02:35.540
"Gulpers eat magic.

49
00:02:36.181 --> 00:02:37.682
Morb was back to being a Void."

50
00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:39.524
Maff nodded.

51
00:02:39.544 --> 00:02:45.008
"Wyssa had decided that a scatter beast would provide too quick and merciful an end to Morb," he

52
00:02:45.048 --> 00:02:48.631
said. "So she decided to strand him on Skellia.

53
00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:53.616
She'd discovered that Morb is terrified of deep water and can't swim."

54
00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:58.750
"Oh!" Now Zann understood Wyssa's plan.

55
00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:04.553
"So she left him there with no magic, which means no way to reach a wormhole or navigate

56
00:03:04.573 --> 00:03:05.213
the vortex."

57
00:03:05.233 --> 00:03:08.075
"Exactly," Maff confirmed.

58
00:03:08.595 --> 00:03:12.577
"There was only a small island left, and the waters were still rising.

59
00:03:13.818 --> 00:03:18.861
She knew that eventually he would drown, but that he'd have plenty of time to ponder his own

60
00:03:18.921 --> 00:03:20.562
demise in the meantime."

61
00:03:20.582 --> 00:03:24.384
"Wow, that's horrible," Gliss said.

62
00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.361
She glanced at the others.

63
00:03:26.381 --> 00:03:27.982
"Even for Morb."

64
00:03:28.002 --> 00:03:30.623
"Yeah." Zann shuddered.

65
00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.964
"So then you found him there?"

66
00:03:33.164 --> 00:03:33.965
he asked Maff.

67
00:03:33.985 --> 00:03:36.266
"That's right," Maff said.

68
00:03:36.286 --> 00:03:40.348
"He begged me to take him away from Skellia.

69
00:03:41.349 --> 00:03:44.731
I wouldn't do that—he still had to pay for his crimes.

70
00:03:45.832 --> 00:03:47.713
But I couldn't help taking pity on him.

71
00:03:48.513 --> 00:03:49.814
I didn't want him to die."

72
00:03:50.654 --> 00:03:53.576
"So you created that houseboat," Zann said.

73
00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:58.682
"Yes. I also provided him with a pair of infused gloves.

74
00:03:59.842 --> 00:04:05.965
They contained just enough self-refreshing magic to allow Morb to create food and other basic necessities."

75
00:04:05.985 --> 00:04:09.366
"Self-refreshing magic?"

76
00:04:09.626 --> 00:04:10.967
Perda sounded curious.

77
00:04:11.527 --> 00:04:12.348
"What do you mean?"

78
00:04:12.368 --> 00:04:16.749
"It's a very simple type of off-world magic," Maff explained.

79
00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.530
"It's rather weak though.

80
00:04:19.211 --> 00:04:25.049
That's why I chose it, given Morb's, er, talents for manipulating magic."

81
00:04:25.069 --> 00:04:27.571
"Wow," Gliss said.

82
00:04:27.591 --> 00:04:31.433
"Now a bunch of stuff makes a lot more sense."

83
00:04:32.613 --> 00:04:34.514
"But not all of it," Zann added.

84
00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:37.996
"Morb only had a weak pair of infused gloves.

85
00:04:38.857 --> 00:04:43.519
So how was he able to do Masking spells and send me weird messages from another world?"

86
00:04:43.539 --> 00:04:46.821
"Good question," Perda said.

87
00:04:46.841 --> 00:04:50.063
"Masking spells take a lot of magic energy.

88
00:04:50.283 --> 00:04:51.784
At least that's what the books say.

89
00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:56.802
And who knows what kind of spell he used to communicate with Zann."

90
00:04:56.822 --> 00:04:59.144
"I have no idea."

91
00:04:59.504 --> 00:05:00.384
Maff shrugged.

92
00:05:00.404 --> 00:05:07.248
"I thought I'd considered every possibility, but clearly my brother is even cleverer than I realized.

93
00:05:08.368 --> 00:05:13.271
He must have harnessed some sort of native Skellian magic source to increase the gloves' power."

94
00:05:13.291 --> 00:05:17.233
"Maybe he caught a gulper or something," Perda suggested.

95
00:05:18.014 --> 00:05:18.974
Darb winced.

96
00:05:18.994 --> 00:05:20.855
"I hope not," he said.

97
00:05:20.875 --> 00:05:25.849
"Or if he did, I hope he treated it better than he did those blue leeches he brought

98
00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:32.332
here." Zann was a little surprised that Darb was so concerned about the gulpers, which were kind of

99
00:05:32.372 --> 00:05:39.655
scary. But Darb did love all animals, from panic bugs to the biggest, nastiest dragons.

100
00:05:39.675 --> 00:05:44.137
"This is looking bad," Gliss declared in a shaky voice.

101
00:05:44.157 --> 00:05:47.619
"We have to tell someone that Morb is on the loose!"

102
00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:49.700
"Who can we tell?"

103
00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:50.460
Perda said.

104
00:05:50.992 --> 00:05:52.673
"First City is in chaos.

105
00:05:53.234 --> 00:05:55.916
Nobody even knows where the king and queen have gone!"

106
00:05:55.936 --> 00:06:01.199
"Yeah, and my parents and Boz wouldn't even listen to us," Zann said.

107
00:06:01.219 --> 00:06:04.382
"That is, before they got tossed in the dungeon."

108
00:06:05.022 --> 00:06:05.863
He looked at Maff.

109
00:06:05.883 --> 00:06:08.044
"Do you think you could get us in to see them?"

110
00:06:09.105 --> 00:06:11.747
"Are you sure that's a good idea?"

111
00:06:11.927 --> 00:06:12.447
Gliss said.

112
00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:15.409
"What if the guards throw us in a cell too?"

113
00:06:15.429 --> 00:06:18.812
"It might be worth the risk," Maff said.

114
00:06:19.192 --> 00:06:22.215
"Boz and Teplo might have a good idea for stopping Morb."

115
00:06:22.235 --> 00:06:26.098
"You mean you don't know how to stop him?"

116
00:06:26.318 --> 00:06:26.858
Perda said.

117
00:06:27.979 --> 00:06:30.121
Maff shook his head and looked grim.

118
00:06:30.141 --> 00:06:32.943
"I'm sorry, I don't.

119
00:06:33.844 --> 00:06:37.347
But I'm willing to do whatever it takes if someone else has a plan."

120
00:06:38.668 --> 00:06:40.529
Zann stared at Maff in alarm.

121
00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:45.834
If Morb's own brother didn't know how to stop him, what chance did they have?

122
00:06:46.995 --> 00:06:48.456
But he tried not to lose hope.

123
00:06:49.217 --> 00:06:51.666
"Okay, let's go to the dungeon," he said.
